    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-6" id="fn-6" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
        <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Calibri',sans-serif;font-size:11pt;font-weight:400;line-height:107%">Discovery Gas Transmission invoices the ACA surcharge and Junction Fee on quantities of gas received from Mainline services only, as all gas transported through Discovery's Gathering facilities and Market Expansion facilities must be transported through the Mainline facilities. Otherwise, shippers would be double billed the ACA surcharges. Therefore, when the Commission develops Discovery's annual charge amount, it should include the volumes from the Mainline transportation services. (The detail appears on page 304 and 305, line 1, 2, 5 and 8 of From 2) For the year 2024, the applicable Mainline transportation quantity is 165,939,602.</span>
      </div>
    </link:footnote>
